        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">wip</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43424",
            "title": "Add a guide on fetch metadata",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-13T00:31:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-13T00:12:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add a \"Client-side considerations\" section to the CORS errors landing page covering three strategies: avoiding preflight via simple requests, using <code class=\"notranslate\">no-cors</code> mode for opaque responses, and proxy servers</li>\n<li>Add a \"If you don't control the server\" section to the <code class=\"notranslate\">CORSMissingAllowOrigin</code> error page pointing to these client-side alternatives</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The CORS error documentation focuses entirely on server-side fixes. Developers who don't control the server have no guidance. A maintainer commented \"Please feel free to change this doc in whatever way you feel appropriate.\"</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #39378.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3037681468\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39378\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39378/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39378\">#39378</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Test plan</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Landing page renders with new section</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> CORSMissingAllowOrigin page renders with new section</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> All internal links resolve</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Code example renders correctly</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43423",
            "title": "Add client-side CORS solutions to error documentation",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-12T23:38:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-12T23:37:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kovan",
                "url": "https://github.com/kovan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add documentation pages for <code class=\"notranslate\">type()</code> instance method on <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Memory</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Table</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Global</code></li>\n<li>These methods are part of the <a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/js-types\">WebAssembly js-types proposal</a> and return objects describing the type of each construct</li>\n<li>List <code class=\"notranslate\">type()</code> in each object's instance methods section on their parent pages</li>\n<li>Follows the existing format established by <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Tag.prototype.type()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The js-types proposal adds <code class=\"notranslate\">type()</code> methods to Memory, Table, and Global, but only <code class=\"notranslate\">Tag.type()</code> is currently documented on MDN. The issue notes these methods are implemented in Safari and meet MDN's documentation criteria.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41157.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3421949146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41157\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41157/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41157\">#41157</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Test plan</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> New pages render correctly</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Browser compatibility tables load (via <code class=\"notranslate\">browser-compat</code> keys)</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Parent page instance method lists link correctly</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43422",
            "title": "Document type() method for Memory, Table, and Global",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-12T23:37:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-12T23:37:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kovan",
                "url": "https://github.com/kovan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add a Description section to the <code class=\"notranslate\">backdrop-filter</code> CSS property page explaining that effects are bounded by the nearest ancestor backdrop root</li>\n<li>List the properties that create a backdrop root: <code class=\"notranslate\">filter</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">opacity</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">mask</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">mask-image</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">mask-border</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">clip-path</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">backdrop-filter</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">mix-blend-mode</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">will-change</code></li>\n<li>Explain the common confusion when <code class=\"notranslate\">backdrop-filter</code> appears to have no effect due to an ancestor backdrop root</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developers are frequently confused when <code class=\"notranslate\">backdrop-filter</code> doesn't affect all pixels behind an element. The concept of a \"backdrop root\" (from Filter Effects Level 2) is not documented on MDN. A previous PR (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3290718617\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40627\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40627/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40627\">#40627</a>) attempted this but was closed due to merge conflicts; this is a fresh implementation incorporating reviewer feedback (using a dedicated Description section instead of a note).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40602.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3286769417\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40602\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40602\">#40602</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Test plan</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Page renders correctly with new Description section</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> All CSS property links resolve</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43421",
            "title": "Document backdrop root concept on backdrop-filter page",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-12T23:37:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-12T23:37:10.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kovan",
                "url": "https://github.com/kovan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add a new guide page (<code class=\"notranslate\">Web/Performance/Guides/bfcache</code>) explaining the back/forward cache</li>\n<li>Covers: how bfcache works, bfcache vs HTTP caching (RFC 9111 Section 6), stale content handling via <code class=\"notranslate\">pageshow</code>, what blocks bfcache (unload, no-store, open connections), monitoring with <code class=\"notranslate\">notRestoredReasons</code>, and best practices</li>\n<li>Links the guide from the Performance landing page and the bfcache glossary entry</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The bfcache glossary entry is brief and doesn't cover how bfcache interacts with HTTP caching, what blocks it, or how to handle stale content. A maintainer requested a full guide page under Web/Performance.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As requested in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3433247968\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41211\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41211/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41211\">#41211</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Test plan</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> New page renders correctly</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> All internal links resolve</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Performance landing page link works</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Glossary entry links work</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43420",
            "title": "Add bfcache guide under Web/Performance",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-12T23:37:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-12T23:36:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kovan",
                "url": "https://github.com/kovan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217326?u=a4cdaefc3a39658f4d104b96ec8c78f10ac63d12&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add a new guide page (<code class=\"notranslate\">Web/API/Push_API/Web_Push_Architecture</code>) explaining how the Web Push infrastructure works end-to-end</li>\n<li>Covers: subscription flow, push services (Mozilla Autopush, FCM, Apple), message encryption (RFC 8291), VAPID authentication (RFC 8292), delivery headers (TTL, Urgency, Topic), response codes, and subscription lifecycle</li>\n<li>Links the new guide from the Push API landing page's See Also section</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The existing Push API docs explain the JavaScript interfaces but not the underlying architecture. Developers need to understand VAPID, encryption, and the delivery protocol to build a working implementation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As requested in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3108081292\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39747\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39747/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39747\">#39747</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Test plan</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> New page renders correctly</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> All internal links resolve</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> See Also link from Push API landing page works</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43419",
            "title": "Add web push architecture guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-13T08:47:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-12T23:36:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kovan",
                "url": "https://github.com/kovan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88993368?u=3e60c7d167b03a8cb435e71361ac5708dee39416&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A new guide for the Properties and Values API section was created in February: <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/commit/98bbdcd90e5487539cebe19b12fe3d731fb5a03e/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/commit/98bbdcd90e5487539cebe19b12fe3d731fb5a03e\"><tt>98bbdcd</tt></a><br>\nBut it wasn't added as a new children link to the CSS Guides sidebar section. I would suggest adding it below the present CSS Houdini link.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This update will bring greater visibility to this excellent guide created by <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/estelle/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/estelle\">@estelle</a> to all users who read the MDN daily.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related pull request commit history: <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/commit/98bbdcd90e5487539cebe19b12fe3d731fb5a03e/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/commit/98bbdcd90e5487539cebe19b12fe3d731fb5a03e\"><tt>98bbdcd</tt></a><br>\nAll credits to Estelle.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Links</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Properties_and_values_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Properties_and_values_API</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Properties_and_values_API/Registering_properties\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Properties_and_values_API/Registering_properties</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43410",
            "title": "Add new registering properties guide as a children to the CSS properties and values API sidebar section.",
